Legitimate credential-adjacent content — none of these may fire.

Placeholders:  password = "${DB_PASSWORD}"   password: <your-password>   password = "changeme"
Masked:        password = "********"
A grep pattern in a hook:  grep -qE "password:|secret:|token:|apiKey:"
Prose about passwords: a password template whose derivation rule survived intact
An env var NAME, not a value: password = "DB_PASSWORD"
A shell reference: PGPASSWORD="$DB_PASSWORD" psql -h localhost
